  "review": {
    "note": "Reviewed all 15 Python and 3 Node direct requirement entries against current registry metadata, including candidates outside the previous bounds. Only h2hdb 0.37.0, build 1.6.1 and Ruff 0.16.7 changed since the previous reviewed receipt; the other external release candidates and their prior compatibility conclusions are unchanged. Compared core 0.36.0 through 0.37.0 source: the breaking source-adapter writer protocol does not change OPDS public read-only catalog APIs, catalog/domain values or schema epoch 3/version 6. Widened the bounded core requirement to >=0.36.0,<0.38.0 without a shim or data migration. The full bounded non-deep suite passed 836 tests on installed PyPI core 0.36.0, including the real 165-publication SQLite HTTP fixture and wheel metadata check. Rebuilt the development environment through the full registry resolver with PyPI core 0.37.0 and all current candidates; 15 SQLite catalog/HTTP and wheel contract tests passed on core 0.37.0. The built-wheel regression accepts both supported core lanes and rejects 0.35.5 and unreviewed 0.38.0. Reviewed build 1.6.1 official tagged CHANGELOG (https://github.com/pypa/build/blob/1.6.1/CHANGELOG.rst): Windows symlink-probe regression fix; reviewed Ruff 0.16.7 release notes (https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases/tag/0.16.7): lint/format fixes and preview additions. Both latest tools are installed and pass the fast gate. All latest direct releases satisfy declared bounds and Python 3.14. Final exact-tree full gate and cohort-level installation checks are reported separately.",
